# inviters.py
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# "מזמין" (the person who invited a visitor) as a managed list instead of free text.
#
# The value still lives where it always did: in the visitor's `properties` JSON, under
# the key the data already uses (default "מזמין"; the key name can be changed in the
# settings, and a few common spellings are recognised too). Nothing about the visitors
# changes just because this module exists. On top of that:
#   * a list of inviters (table `inviters`), managed by an admin;
#   * an admin switch "an inviter is required" (like the information-security switch):
#     when on, saving a visitor needs an inviter chosen from the list, and the stored
#     text is the list's spelling;
#   * a migration from the existing free text: a preview groups the values that differ
#     only in spaces / letter case, "add to the list" is non-destructive, and
#     "unify spelling" rewrites those visitors' value to the list's spelling (backup first);
#   * reports and statistics group by the inviter, matching the free text to the list
#     ignoring spaces and letter case, so they are right even before any rewrite.
#
#   GET    /inviters                          list + switch + key   (visitor/report viewers)
#   POST   /inviters                          add                   (admin.settings)
#   PUT    /inviters/{id}                     rename / (de)activate (admin.settings)
#   DELETE /inviters/{id}                     remove from the list  (admin.settings)
#   PUT    /inviters/config                   switch + key name     (admin.settings)
#   GET    /inviters/migration/preview        what the data holds   (admin.settings)
#   POST   /inviters/migration/apply          add to list / unify   (admin.settings)
# ------------------------------------------------------------

